{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Persist the currently supplied DNS nameserver on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The initial live configuration showed 10.100.61.1 as the sole supplied IPv4 DNS server. It was stored in the autoconnecting NetworkManager profile, remained active in the resolver, and survived a confirmed reboot with DNS resolution working afterward.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e105cb43401d4cab","cmd-f2719a29ac99431a","cmd-cf9a88b4f8334f70","cmd-793fa6d470c14a11","cmd-c4cd91593e324396","cmd-dfa0953f41364b5d","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Add infra.test as the persistent system search domain on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The domain was absent initially, then appeared in both the persistent NetworkManager profile and NetworkManager-generated /etc/resolv.conf. Those settings remained present after the confirmed reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e105cb43401d4cab","cmd-f2719a29ac99431a","cmd-cf9a88b4f8334f70","cmd-793fa6d470c14a11","cmd-c4cd91593e324396","cmd-dfa0953f41364b5d"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The NetworkManager profile modification directly established the requested persistent settings, reapplication activated them for bounded verification, and the scheduled reboot fulfilled the mandatory restart protocol while directly testing persistence. The transient reboot unit did not remain after reboot. All other commands were read-only observations or bounded waiting. Final snapshots show no failed services, package damage, unexpected sockets, or executor-created temporary-file residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f500d5944efd455e","cmd-cdf834b54d3c4bcd","cmd-793fa6d470c14a11","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"Both task outcomes are fully satisfied. Evidence establishes the original supplied DNS value, the persistent profile and live resolver state, a healthy pre-restart baseline, reboot acknowledgement and observable disconnect, a changed boot identity independently corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered NetworkManager connectivity and DNS resolution.","limitations":[]}
